# {{ project_name }} — build output

Everything in this directory is generated by `osprey build`, and every build
recreates it from scratch. Nothing durable lives here: deleting this directory
is always safe, and an edit made here is lost on the next build.

The files you own live one level up, beside `profile.yml`:

- `profile.yml` — what to build; edit this, then run `osprey build`
- `data/channel_limits.json` — per-channel write limits, yours to edit
- `README.md` — how the repo is laid out and operated

What is rendered here: `config.yml` (the resolved settings), the agent's
`.claude/` tree (rules, hooks, and MCP server wiring), and a working copy of
your `data/` files.
